On Jun 21, 7:23 pm, funcrunch <web-goog...@funcrunch.org> wrote:
> This reminds me of a bug around v.3.1.2 where water on a level would,
> under certain circumstances, cause all scrolls, books, and potions
> lying on the floor to go blank eventually. (Yes, I've been playing for
> a long time...)

     It was in 3.1.0; doc/fixes31.1 included with the sources mentions
fixing that.  It would only happen if there was an item in the water
somewhere on the level (and kelp wasn't present yet, so no objects got
placed in water during level creation).  All items on a level's floor
are linked together in a list, and the bug caused every thing which
happened to be past the one in the water to get inflicted with water
damage, first when the wet one went in and then every time that level
got saved and restored (which happens whenever you leave a level and
return to it as well as when an explicit save is performed).    The
save/restore handling is what usually caused things to eventually get
rusty or go blank, since they have a respectable chance--especially
when your Luck is high--to avoid damage each time some is attempted.

     The bug gave rise to a myth that this was intended behavior of
"damp levels".  And it was most noticeable if the Book of the Dead
happened to follow a submerged item, because that triggered a message
about steam rising (to indicate that wetness wasn't affecting it)
every time the relevant level was revisited or the game was restored.


